  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Agroforestry Development &#x2013; Moringa</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This project explores the feasibility, economic viability, and sustainability of producing organic moringa in Angola for both local consumption and export to the Netherlands and other European countries. Moringa, with its nutritional benefits and diverse applications, holds promise for Angolan farmers.However, challenges include a lack of export knowledge and competitive analysis for the European market. Addressing these gaps could significantly boost Angola&apos;s agricultural sector, contributing to economic diversification and poverty reduction.The feasibility study will help both Dutch and Angolan stakeholders in the moringa value chain to set up trade Dutch beneficiaries include investors, consultancies and importers. The study should therefore be shared with these relevant and potentially potentially interested stakeholders in Angola and the Netherlands.</narrative>
  </description>
